        "Aestivation: Arrangement of sepals/petals in bud. 1. Valvate: sepals/petals touch margins without overlapping (Calotropis); 2. Twisted: one margin overlaps that of next (China rose, Lady's finger, Cotton); 3. Imbricate: margins overlap but not in any particular direction (Cassia, Gulmohur); 4. Vexillary / Papilionaceous: largest posterior petal Vexillum overlaps 2 lateral wings (Alae), which overlap 2 smallest anterior fused keels (Carina) (Pea, Bean, Fabaceae).",
